## 4.2 Sparklines with gtExtras

### 4.2.1 Preparing the data


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
report <- coffeechain %>%
  mutate(Year = year(Date)) %>%
  filter(Year == "2013") %>%
  mutate(Month = month(Date, label = TRUE, abbr = TRUE)) %>%
  group_by(Product, Month) %>%
  summarise(Sales = sum(Sales)) %>%
  ungroup()

head(report)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
# A tibble: 6 × 3
  Product  Month Sales
  <chr>    <ord> <dbl>
1 Amaretto Jan    1210
2 Amaretto Feb    1144
3 Amaretto Mar    1100
4 Amaretto Apr    1117
5 Amaretto May    1057
6 Amaretto Jun    1059
```


:::
:::


`gt_plt_sparkline()` expects the values as a list-column, so I collapse each
product's monthly sales into a list.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize(`Monthly Sales` = list(Sales), .groups = "drop")
```

